thy (18% error rate), and v3.3.0 was its last healthy release. Rolling back.", "reasoning_content": "payments-worker v3.4.0 is unhealthy, v3.3.0 was healthy. Rollback to v3.3.0.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150b179c6738f8f6e75b0", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-worker\",\"version\":\"v3.3.0\"}", "name": "rollback"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150b181467745b8dc6830", "function": {"arguments": "{\"idempotency_key\":\"sev2-payments-worker-v3.4.0-regression-rollback\",\"severity\":\"SEV2\",\"service\":\"payments-worker\",\"summary\":\"v3.4.0 release this morning caused errors in payments-worker (unhealthy, ~18% error rate across us-east/us-west/eu-west). Rolled back production to v3.3.0 (last healthy release), which was approved and rolled out to all regions. Root cause of the v3.4.0 regression still to be investigated.\",\"title\":\"Payments errors after this morning's deploy of payments-worker v3.4.0 (rolled back to v3.3.0)\"}", "name": "create_incident"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150b182b8766ab580aa1e", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments-worker\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "stop", "content": "## Summary\n\n**Issue:** This morning's deploy of **payments-worker v3.4.0** caused production errors (~18% error rate, service unhealthy).\n\n**Actions taken:**\n1. Initially investigated `payments` / `payments-api` \u2014 the first rollback attempt on `payments-api` was denied by the human approver, who pointed to `payments-worker` as the actual source of the problem.\n2. Confirmed payments-worker v3.4.0 was unhealthy and v3.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n3. **Rolled back payments-worker to v3.3.0** \u2014 approved and rolled out to all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west).\n4. **Opened SEV2 incident INC-0001** \u2014 on-call has been paged.\n\n**Current state:** payments-worker is back on v3.3.0 and healthy again (error rate dropped from 18% \u2192 0.2%). The root cause of the v3.4.0 regression remains open for investigation under INC-0001.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": []}]}